WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:08.717 --> 00:00:11.344
[intriguing music playing]

2
00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:13.972
[detective 1] We're trying to collect
as much information as we can

3
00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:17.851
to get a clear picture on what's going on
and figure out where to start. okay?

4
00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:21.229
-[Jack] Okay.
-[detective 1] Um… Starting yesterday.

5
00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:23.898
-did you go to the football game?
-[Jack] No. I was at work.

6
00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:26.568
[detective 1] What did you do
after you got off shift?

7
00:00:26.651 --> 00:00:28.737
[Jack] I went home

8
00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:32.490
and met up with my friends.
and then we went to the Corner Club.

9
00:00:34.075 --> 00:00:37.746
[Anthony] We identified Jack
as the ex-boyfriend of Kaylee.

10
00:00:38.246 --> 00:00:42.333
He was very open and honest about
his knowledge of what was going on.

11
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:46.004
He explained their history
between he and Kaylee.

12
00:00:46.087 --> 00:00:50.592
and how their relationship was.
and how long it lasted. and how it ended.

13
00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:53.219
[Jack] Eventually. I came back home.

14
00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:56.389
-[detective 1] Have roommates? They there?
-[Jack] Mm-hm. Yeah.

15
00:00:56.473 --> 00:00:59.350
[officer 1] What time did you guys
make it home from the bar?

16
00:00:59.851 --> 00:01:01.519
[man] 1:30ish.

17
00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:04.022
-[officer 1] You were with him all night?
-[man] Mm-hmm.

18
00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:09.194
[Anthony] And so. through following up
on some of the evidence that he shared

19
00:01:09.277 --> 00:01:13.364
of his whereabouts
and his alibis for that evening.

20
00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:16.159
we were able to eliminate him
as a potential suspect.

21
00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:19.579
[detective 1] You're not in trouble.
I just gotta ask questions.

22
00:01:19.662 --> 00:01:22.373
Talk me through the rest of your evening.
You guys hang out?

23
00:01:22.457 --> 00:01:25.126
[Jack] I came back home.
Pretty much just went to bed.

24
00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:29.214
[detective 1] You had missed calls from
Kaylee. Remember what time. by chance?

25
00:01:29.297 --> 00:01:33.009
[Jack] Yeah. they were.
like. between 2:40 and 3:00.

26
00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.595
The last one was. like. 2:57.

27
00:01:35.678 --> 00:01:39.182
Kaylee has called me and stuff.
like. if she's walking home.

28
00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.850
and she thinks someone. like.

29
00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:44.896
is watching or following her.
she'll call me and just…

30
00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:48.108
-Just to have someone on the phone.
-[detective 1] Yeah. yeah.

31
00:01:48.191 --> 00:01:51.152
Did she ever mention that
she thought someone was following her.

32
00:01:51.236 --> 00:01:53.446
or was it more just getting creeped out?

33
00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.323
[Jack] Yeah. just got creeped out.

34
00:01:56.199 --> 00:02:00.578
Um. ever had any roommates
complain about anyone stalking them?

35
00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:01.663
[Bethany] Mm-mm.

36
00:02:02.163 --> 00:02:06.543
Once though. Kaylee said
when everyone was. like. gone

37
00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.254
and it was only Kaylee
and she was taking Murphy out.

38
00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.299
and she said she swears
she saw someone staring at her

39
00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:16.136
while she was taking the dog out to pee.

40
00:02:18.054 --> 00:02:21.266
She could see. like.
a man's silhouette staring at her.

41
00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:25.478
-Know how long ago that was?
-[Bethany] Maybe like a month.

42
00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:28.648
[intriguing music continues]

43
00:02:28.731 --> 00:02:31.192
[Dylan] About a week ago.
our door is broken

44
00:02:31.276 --> 00:02:35.280
but me. Maddie and Bethany got home
and the door was wide open.

45
00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:38.783
[detective 2] Did you ever. uh.
find the back slider open or anything?

46
00:02:38.867 --> 00:02:42.245
-Is that usually locked?
-[Dylan] We're pretty good at locking it.

47
00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:45.039
I don't think we locked it last night.

48
00:02:46.374 --> 00:02:49.627
[Jack] There's a lot of people coming in
and out of their house all the time

49
00:02:49.711 --> 00:02:52.297
just because they're well-liked people.

50
00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.551
[detective 3] This may seem like
a weird question.

51
00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.928
but who would do something like this?

52
00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:02.056
[Dylan] I couldn't even imagine.

53
00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.142
[tense music playing]

54
00:03:07.103 --> 00:03:09.439
[music swelling]

55
00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.526
[music becomes quiet]

56
00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.490
[music fades]

57
00:03:21.451 --> 00:03:23.536
[intriguing music playing]

58
00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.122
[Ed] During the time
of the Moscow homicides.

59
00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:30.293
I was a Special Agent in the
Coeur d'Alene resident agency of the FBI.

60
00:03:30.835 --> 00:03:35.048
Moscow PD just needed a lot of resources
at a moment's notice.

61
00:03:35.131 --> 00:03:39.093
I drove down to Moscow.
walked into Chief Fry's office

62
00:03:39.177 --> 00:03:44.182
and offered assistance. and explained
what we could do from the FBI standpoint.

63
00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:46.643
The chief told us. "Bring it."

64
00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:52.774
and that's where we came in
to assist the investigation.

65
00:03:54.192 --> 00:03:58.696
[detective 4] We're just trying
to put the pieces of the puzzle together.

66
00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:01.324
um. just with everything that's going on.

67
00:04:01.824 --> 00:04:05.036
[Anthony] Everybody who had
any information.

68
00:04:05.119 --> 00:04:07.330
we needed to talk to them.
to interview them.

69
00:04:08.039 --> 00:04:12.710
[Ed] In this particular case.
we did not have a clear intended victim.

70
00:04:12.794 --> 00:04:16.464
You don't just have a single homicide.
you have four different kids.

71
00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.884
[Anthony] Immediately.
we dug into the personal relationships

72
00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.344
of each of the victims.

73
00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:25.223
We're gonna go back and try
to get a little bit of the timeline. okay?

74
00:04:25.306 --> 00:04:26.182
[Bethany] Yeah.

75
00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.934
[Ed] We call it "victimology."

76
00:04:28.017 --> 00:04:30.395
investigating the lives of the victims.

77
00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:32.605
Tracking friends. tracking family.

78
00:04:33.189 --> 00:04:36.943
tracking movement to determine
who they've come across

79
00:04:37.026 --> 00:04:41.072
that has a problem with them.
has a motive to actually hurt them.

80
00:04:41.656 --> 00:04:44.200
[Anthony] To do that.
we needed to create a timeline

81
00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:46.953
of that evening
and into the early hours of that morning.

82
00:04:47.036 --> 00:04:49.622
and try to find some sort of a connection.

83
00:04:49.706 --> 00:04:52.083
[detective 2] When was the last time
that you were over at…?

84
00:04:52.166 --> 00:04:55.086
[Hunter J.] The last time
before today was yesterday.

85
00:04:55.169 --> 00:04:59.007
[detective 2] Okay.
What were you doing there yesterday?

86
00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:03.386
[Hunter J.] We were pre-gaming
the football game for the Vandals.

87
00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.721
[detective 2] Gotcha.

88
00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.850
[Hunter J.] We left their house
and went to a different apartment

89
00:05:08.933 --> 00:05:10.310
at roughly. like. 2:30.

90
00:05:10.893 --> 00:05:12.770
[people shouting]

91
00:05:14.063 --> 00:05:16.649
[Kristi] Saturday it was a football game.

92
00:05:16.733 --> 00:05:19.068
There was a lot of people in town.

93
00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:21.154
It was the last home game of the year.

94
00:05:21.237 --> 00:05:22.905
Kaylee was really excited about it.

95
00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:26.242
She texted me a picture of her and Maddie.

96
00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.788
And I replied. "My lovies!"

97
00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:35.668
And then she called me.
and I had bought her some succulents.

98
00:05:35.752 --> 00:05:37.503
She had to tell me quick

99
00:05:37.587 --> 00:05:40.673
this rambling little story
of how the succulents were doing.

100
00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:42.925
She said. "Mom.
we're gonna come home take a nap

101
00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:44.427
and gonna go out tonight."

102
00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:45.970
[intriguing music continues]

103
00:05:46.054 --> 00:05:49.057
And I said. "Okay. have fun!
I love you guys."

104
00:05:50.224 --> 00:05:53.019
[Peter] That day.
I went and pre-gamed with Ethan.

105
00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:56.272
We hung out on the couch and had a beer.

106
00:05:56.356 --> 00:06:00.068
And Ethan was upset
that I was leaving the pre-game.

107
00:06:00.151 --> 00:06:02.570
He was like.
"Screw it. Can I just come with you?"

108
00:06:03.154 --> 00:06:07.575
Later in that night.
we went to Kappa Alpha Theta's formal.

109
00:06:07.658 --> 00:06:10.912
Ethan's sister.
Maizie's in that sorority. also.

110
00:06:10.995 --> 00:06:14.832
Ethan was a triplet.
He was inseparable from his siblings.

111
00:06:15.416 --> 00:06:20.046
Maizie didn't have a date.
so Maizie took Ethan as her date.

112
00:06:20.922 --> 00:06:22.757
We went to that formal. That was fun.

113
00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.551
That was one of
the funnest nights of my life.

114
00:06:26.511 --> 00:06:28.262
Xana didn't go to that.

115
00:06:28.346 --> 00:06:30.932
She kinda did her own thing
until after the formal.

116
00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:35.228
[Bethany] We were just hanging out
at our house.

117
00:06:35.311 --> 00:06:37.939
Ethan was at formal
because he went with his sister

118
00:06:38.022 --> 00:06:39.607
because she didn't have a date.

119
00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:42.402
And then he came over
and then we all walked over together.

120
00:06:42.485 --> 00:06:44.153
And the last time you saw

121
00:06:45.196 --> 00:06:47.532
Xana and Ethan was at the Sigma Chi house?

122
00:06:47.615 --> 00:06:49.075
-Mm.
-Okay.

123
00:06:49.158 --> 00:06:52.412
You. Ethan. Xana…
Was there another person with you?

124
00:06:52.495 --> 00:06:55.706
-Or just three of you that walked?
-Uh. Maddie walked over with us.

125
00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.751
[Cooper] I remember hanging out
with Ethan and Xana that night.

126
00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:01.879
I remember talking about his family.

127
00:07:01.963 --> 00:07:03.840
and being grateful for that conversation.

128
00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:06.968
And something that. I don't know why
God gave me this moment.

129
00:07:07.051 --> 00:07:11.305
but I hugged them both
and I said. "I love you both." Um…

130
00:07:11.389 --> 00:07:13.474
That's something I'll never forget.

131
00:07:13.558 --> 00:07:15.059
Were you guys all together.

132
00:07:15.143 --> 00:07:17.478
or just kind of mingling
throughout the house?

133
00:07:17.562 --> 00:07:19.730
We were all pretty much together

134
00:07:19.814 --> 00:07:23.234
and then Maddie left
to go to the club with Kaylee.

135
00:07:26.404 --> 00:07:29.782
[Alivea] At this point.
we're still driving to my parents' house.

136
00:07:29.866 --> 00:07:32.118
My kids are sleeping in the back here.

137
00:07:32.201 --> 00:07:36.789
I have nothing but time.
I keep going through Kaylee's phone logs.

138
00:07:36.873 --> 00:07:40.168
And I just start texting
some phone numbers

139
00:07:40.251 --> 00:07:42.628
of people that she had communicated with.

140
00:07:42.712 --> 00:07:45.923
"You talked to my sister at 1:07 a.m.?"

141
00:07:46.007 --> 00:07:48.676
Someone would tell me.
"Yes. I did. I was told this.

142
00:07:48.759 --> 00:07:51.846
but so-and-so might have more
information. here's their number."

143
00:07:52.513 --> 00:07:54.015
So I would contact so-and-so.

144
00:07:54.515 --> 00:07:56.934
I'm just trying to find anything I can.

145
00:07:57.518 --> 00:08:03.816
I reach out to the driver who had given
Kaylee and Maddie a ride out that night

146
00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:06.235
and then also take them
back home that night.

147
00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:10.156
I learned from this individual
sometime shortly after 10:00 p.m.

148
00:08:10.239 --> 00:08:11.949
They were picked up to go out.

149
00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:15.411
and this driver dropped them off
at the Corner Club.

150
00:08:15.912 --> 00:08:17.205
[detective 1] What happened next?

151
00:08:17.955 --> 00:08:20.333
[Jack] I did run into Kaylee
at the Corner Club.

152
00:08:20.416 --> 00:08:24.378
said hi to her. talked to her
for probably a minute or so.

153
00:08:26.088 --> 00:08:29.717
I don't even really remember what our…
We had a 30-second conversation.

154
00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:30.885
[detective 1] Okay.

155
00:08:30.968 --> 00:08:33.304
Did it seem normal? Did it seem off?

156
00:08:33.387 --> 00:08:36.140
-[Jack] Yeah. everything seemed normal.
-[detective 1] Okay.

157
00:08:37.892 --> 00:08:39.769
[detective 5] So. what…

158
00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:41.437
Let's go a little bit more.

159
00:08:41.521 --> 00:08:43.564
[Bethany] They went to Grub Truck
after the club.

160
00:08:43.648 --> 00:08:44.649
Okay.

161
00:08:47.151 --> 00:08:50.905
[Maya] Outside the Corner Club.
there's this little. uh. food truck

162
00:08:50.988 --> 00:08:52.406
called the Grub Truck.

163
00:08:53.241 --> 00:08:55.618
Disgusting if you're sober.
If you're drunk. it's phenomenal.

164
00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:58.162
-I understand.
-Pizza mac? You got it.

165
00:08:58.246 --> 00:09:01.999
[Anthony] We had found out that Kaylee
and Maddie had been to the Grub Truck.

166
00:09:02.083 --> 00:09:06.629
We at the police department had been aware
that they had a Twitch feed.

167
00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:10.758
which is an online video feed
of their business. basically.

168
00:09:10.841 --> 00:09:13.844
And people are able to go on there
and make comments.

169
00:09:13.928 --> 00:09:18.599
and we'd utilized that information
through them previously for other cases.

170
00:09:18.683 --> 00:09:23.771
You know. we've had things go on downtown
that maybe got captured on that camera.

171
00:09:23.854 --> 00:09:26.232
so we knew
we definitely needed to look at that.

172
00:09:26.315 --> 00:09:28.192
[intriguing music continues]

173
00:09:28.276 --> 00:09:30.820
[Alivea] I didn't know to look
organically. Someone tipped me off

174
00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:34.490
that this Grub Truck did this.
Maybe it caught Kaylee and Maddie on it.

175
00:09:34.574 --> 00:09:38.286
I just start watching.
you know. just fast-forwarding bits.

176
00:09:38.369 --> 00:09:39.453
-Hello!
-Hi.

177
00:09:39.537 --> 00:09:40.538
Welcome back.

178
00:09:40.621 --> 00:09:43.833
Thanks. I think I would like the. um…

179
00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:46.544
[Alivea] Kaylee and Maddie
come into the screen.

180
00:09:46.627 --> 00:09:49.380
I'm able to recognize them right away.

181
00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:53.634
Everything to me is looking fairly normal.

182
00:09:54.218 --> 00:09:57.471
[Anthony] We watched Kaylee and Maddie
appearing to be very happy

183
00:09:57.555 --> 00:10:00.474
and just enjoying the rest
of their late evening.

184
00:10:00.558 --> 00:10:01.934
They were ordering some food.

185
00:10:02.018 --> 00:10:05.187
but we as investigators
aren't particularly focused on that.

186
00:10:05.271 --> 00:10:07.064
We're looking at
what's going on around them

187
00:10:07.148 --> 00:10:09.317
and what are the other people doing
around them.

188
00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:14.196
and there were some things going on
that would raise suspicion.

189
00:10:14.989 --> 00:10:18.326
We recognized this male in a hood.
hooded sweatshirt.

190
00:10:18.409 --> 00:10:21.162
"Hoodie Guy." as he was coined.

191
00:10:22.163 --> 00:10:24.665
Approached them. spoke to them briefly.

192
00:10:25.625 --> 00:10:29.128
And then once the girls walked out
of view of the camera.

193
00:10:29.211 --> 00:10:32.632
we could see that
this individual in a hoodie followed them.

194
00:10:32.715 --> 00:10:36.844
So. we're gonna look at that and go.
"Okay. there might be something there."

195
00:10:36.927 --> 00:10:39.263
We needed to find more video surveillance

196
00:10:39.347 --> 00:10:42.308
of this individual
in a hoodie in the area.

197
00:10:47.188 --> 00:10:50.733
[reporter] I've been here in Moscow
on scene since about 3:00 p.m.

198
00:10:51.233 --> 00:10:54.153
Since I've been here.
I've watched Moscow police cars

199
00:10:54.236 --> 00:10:56.238
come in and out of this neighborhood

200
00:10:56.322 --> 00:10:58.824
where officials found four people dead.

201
00:11:03.287 --> 00:11:05.247
[officer 1] Well. it's all over the news.

202
00:11:05.331 --> 00:11:09.752
The rumor out there is
somebody died here from fentanyl.

203
00:11:11.462 --> 00:11:15.132
And then somebody else said
somebody might have got stabbed.

204
00:11:15.675 --> 00:11:18.260
I said.
"Well. I can't confirm any of that."

205
00:11:19.345 --> 00:11:21.722
So… But the rumors are out there.

206
00:11:21.806 --> 00:11:22.807
Oh. yeah.

207
00:11:23.516 --> 00:11:26.686
Yeah. there were rumors being spread
all over the place

208
00:11:26.769 --> 00:11:31.941
about maybe it was drugs
or some sort of connection with cartels.

209
00:11:32.983 --> 00:11:35.152
-[officer 2] Are you guys out of here?
-Yeah.

210
00:11:35.236 --> 00:11:37.488
-[officer 2] I'll mark you off.
-All right.

211
00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:42.868
[Anthony] Of course. we didn't know
who the target was. what the motive was.

212
00:11:42.952 --> 00:11:45.121
But it was pretty apparent to us that

213
00:11:45.204 --> 00:11:48.332
for an individual to go into a residence

214
00:11:48.416 --> 00:11:51.627
and kill four people with an edged weapon.

215
00:11:52.545 --> 00:11:53.879
that was purposeful.

216
00:11:53.963 --> 00:11:56.132
[moody dramatic music playing]

217
00:12:00.386 --> 00:12:02.304
[Kristi] We didn't know
what to do. There's…

218
00:12:04.557 --> 00:12:05.516
just shock.

219
00:12:05.599 --> 00:12:12.356
Everyone was coming
to me and Kristi for answers.

220
00:12:12.857 --> 00:12:17.111
We were looking very forward to
seeing somebody who was actually there.

221
00:12:17.194 --> 00:12:20.406
-So. Jack shows up at our house.
-The next day.

222
00:12:20.489 --> 00:12:24.577
[Steve] And we're basically
more like bees. We swarmed him.

223
00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:27.413
He came into the house
and we said. "What's going on?"

224
00:12:27.496 --> 00:12:30.791
Jack couldn't get a hold of us
because they took his phone.

225
00:12:30.875 --> 00:12:34.253
The day before. at the police station.
obviously they were questioning him.

226
00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:39.091
We went through. "What did they do?
Did they interview? What did they say?"

227
00:12:39.175 --> 00:12:42.136
What do you know?
What was she doing? Where was she going?

228
00:12:42.219 --> 00:12:44.889
Jack said. "All I know is this."

229
00:12:44.972 --> 00:12:49.393
He said he was sitting in the hall
of the police department. I'm imagining.

230
00:12:49.894 --> 00:12:53.856
And there are several people there
waiting to talk to the police.

231
00:12:55.357 --> 00:12:56.567
And he overheard…

232
00:12:57.735 --> 00:13:01.530
Dylan talking
to what he assumed was her parents.

233
00:13:02.239 --> 00:13:07.953
Somewhere in the night. Dylan saw a man
all dressed in black with a mask.

234
00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:11.415
And I said. "An intruder?"

235
00:13:11.499 --> 00:13:14.126
"You're telling me there was…"
I remember using that word.

236
00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:17.671
"There was an intruder.
Came into their house. was in the house."

237
00:13:17.755 --> 00:13:20.090
And he's like.
"I don't know. Kristi. I don't know."

238
00:13:20.174 --> 00:13:23.385
I'm like. "Jack. you gotta… you know."
and he's just frazzled.

239
00:13:23.469 --> 00:13:26.514
He's. like. you know.
piecing things together.

240
00:13:26.597 --> 00:13:28.891
He doesn't want
and say something that's not true.

241
00:13:28.974 --> 00:13:30.518
He's like. "That's all I remember."

242
00:13:30.601 --> 00:13:33.354
[dramatic music playing]

243
00:13:34.396 --> 00:13:36.315
[reporter] It was a solemn day
here in Moscow.

244
00:13:36.398 --> 00:13:40.277
A campus ordinarily packed with students
and energy. quiet and empty.

245
00:13:40.861 --> 00:13:42.988
Many trying to process this tragedy.

246
00:13:43.864 --> 00:13:46.909
It was an uneasy feeling
at the University of Idaho.

247
00:13:48.369 --> 00:13:52.039
[Cooper] People are trying to piece
together who. what. where. why. how.

248
00:13:52.665 --> 00:13:55.793
[Peter] All the guys in the house
were kinda restless.

249
00:13:55.876 --> 00:14:00.756
walking around the courtyard talking.
like. "What the hell happened?"

250
00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:04.176
[Cooper] Then I went home
that following day.

251
00:14:05.386 --> 00:14:08.389
which most of everyone did.

252
00:14:08.472 --> 00:14:09.932
No one wanted to be there.

253
00:14:10.432 --> 00:14:12.434
[melancholic music playing]

254
00:14:15.312 --> 00:14:17.064
[Tami] As family. we all gathered.

255
00:14:17.147 --> 00:14:21.527
We all. you know.
talk about it. cry about it.

256
00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:25.990
Try to eat. try to get Kristi to eat.
you know. try to take care of each other.

257
00:14:26.073 --> 00:14:29.076
It was horrible here.

258
00:14:29.159 --> 00:14:32.913
It was horrible. Kristi lost her daughter.

259
00:14:33.414 --> 00:14:35.416
You know. my son lost his daughter.

260
00:14:36.625 --> 00:14:38.502
The girls lost their sibling.

261
00:14:39.128 --> 00:14:40.421
their sister.

262
00:14:40.504 --> 00:14:45.926
♪ Happy birthday. dear Kaylee
Happy bir… ♪

263
00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:51.765
Moscow PD is contacting my dad
via phone call. I think most of the time.

264
00:14:51.849 --> 00:14:55.394
with whatever information.

265
00:14:55.477 --> 00:14:56.770
There's not a whole lot.

266
00:14:58.022 --> 00:15:00.441
We didn't find out their…

267
00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:04.445
manner of death until…

268
00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:09.617
I think. 48 hours after it had happened.

269
00:15:11.493 --> 00:15:15.039
[Tami] Kristi called me.
and I said. "What's going on?"

270
00:15:15.122 --> 00:15:17.041
And she goes.
"We found out what happened."

271
00:15:17.124 --> 00:15:19.209
I was like. "What? Were they shot?"

272
00:15:20.252 --> 00:15:22.087
She says. "No. they were stabbed."

273
00:15:22.171 --> 00:15:25.716
And I was like.
"What? What do you mean?"

274
00:15:25.799 --> 00:15:28.636
She said. "They were all stabbed to death.
we were told today."

275
00:15:28.719 --> 00:15:29.637
And I was like…

276
00:15:31.764 --> 00:15:33.849
[haltingly] I don't even think. like.

277
00:15:33.933 --> 00:15:36.685
you don't know what to think
when someone tells you that.

278
00:15:37.394 --> 00:15:40.230
[Kristi] The coroner called me
and confirmed to us

279
00:15:40.314 --> 00:15:43.400
that Maddie and Kaylee
were in bed together.

280
00:15:43.484 --> 00:15:46.779
and that a very large knife

281
00:15:47.279 --> 00:15:49.281
with a seven-inch blade

282
00:15:50.032 --> 00:15:51.200
was used.

283
00:15:51.283 --> 00:15:52.201
Yeah.

284
00:15:53.452 --> 00:15:55.537
[Jeff] I just couldn't understand that.

285
00:15:55.621 --> 00:15:57.790
[melancholic music continues]

286
00:15:57.873 --> 00:16:02.294
It's just such a wrong thing…
to. to have to deal with.

287
00:16:02.378 --> 00:16:04.254
and it's everybody's worst nightmare.

288
00:16:04.964 --> 00:16:09.510
The night of the 12th and the 13th.
I was at the WSU game with Jazzmin.

289
00:16:09.593 --> 00:16:11.303
I was thinking. "You know what?"

290
00:16:12.137 --> 00:16:15.432
"I should give Xana a call.
Maybe I'll stay at her house tonight."

291
00:16:17.851 --> 00:16:20.562
And I kinda thought about it.

292
00:16:21.897 --> 00:16:26.485
And I drank quite a bit that night.
And I go. "You know what?"

293
00:16:27.361 --> 00:16:31.657
"Xana'd probably get mad
if I drove over there." so I didn't go.

294
00:16:32.825 --> 00:16:35.703
But I could've gone.
and things would have been different.

295
00:16:38.038 --> 00:16:39.915
Maybe they would've
had a chance. you know?

296
00:16:40.582 --> 00:16:41.709
Some of them.

297
00:16:43.252 --> 00:16:44.253
Yeah.

298
00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:49.216
[ominous music playing]

299
00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:53.595
[news anchor 1] Let's turn to new details
in the case that is gripping the nation.

300
00:16:53.679 --> 00:16:57.016
the shocking murders
of four University of Idaho students.

301
00:16:57.099 --> 00:17:00.894
Yeah. days after their tragic deaths.
police have yet to identify a suspect.

302
00:17:00.978 --> 00:17:04.189
and it's left a small college town
on edge this morning.

303
00:17:05.232 --> 00:17:09.737
[Ed] Majority of homicide cases.
a suspect appears quickly.

304
00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:11.113
[knocking on door]

305
00:17:12.531 --> 00:17:17.494
When you get into something like this
where it just isn't happening.

306
00:17:18.287 --> 00:17:21.457
this is what in law enforcement
we refer to the "whodunnit."

307
00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:27.671
where you don't have
a fairly immediate suspect in the case.

308
00:17:28.756 --> 00:17:31.550
The word's getting out.
the pressures come.

309
00:17:31.633 --> 00:17:33.302
and the answers aren't there yet.

310
00:17:34.887 --> 00:17:37.222
And so. you start expanding out.

311
00:17:37.806 --> 00:17:40.768
[news anchor 2] Law enforcement's
latest efforts have been sifting through

312
00:17:40.851 --> 00:17:42.811
surveillance videos from downtown

313
00:17:42.895 --> 00:17:45.856
and any doorbell cameras
in the area of the crime scene.

314
00:17:45.939 --> 00:17:48.776
[news anchor 3]
Volunteers put up flyers on store windows

315
00:17:48.859 --> 00:17:52.237
asking anyone who has
a home camera. a security camera.

316
00:17:52.321 --> 00:17:55.491
to look for anything suspicious
the night of the murders.

317
00:17:55.574 --> 00:17:59.828
We were able to gather
every bit of video footage

318
00:17:59.912 --> 00:18:03.874
from that time frame
in the entire Moscow area.

319
00:18:04.541 --> 00:18:07.086
[Anthony] We had detectives
sitting for hours on end

320
00:18:07.169 --> 00:18:10.547
-re-watching footage over and over again.
-[dramatic music playing]

321
00:18:10.631 --> 00:18:15.636
We were able to work with all of the folks
involved in the Grub Truck video.

322
00:18:15.719 --> 00:18:19.306
There were lots of people around. We ended
up identifying all of those people.

323
00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:21.975
We were able to identify Hoodie Guy.

324
00:18:23.185 --> 00:18:25.771
-[Hathaway] This is Sergeant Hathaway.
-[Hoodie Guy] How's it going?

325
00:18:25.854 --> 00:18:27.147
[Hathaway] How we doing?

326
00:18:27.815 --> 00:18:31.276
-[Hoodie Guy] I want to make a statement.
-[Hathaway] Okay. what's going on?

327
00:18:32.236 --> 00:18:36.365
[Hoodie Guy] I'm just friends with Maddie.
I was with her at the bar that night.

328
00:18:36.448 --> 00:18:41.703
We left to get Grub Truck. and then
she got picked up in a silver Sedan.

329
00:18:42.246 --> 00:18:47.000
That's my only description I know.
And then they went home from there.

330
00:18:47.709 --> 00:18:52.548
All of the information that he gave
showed us that he was not involved.

331
00:18:52.631 --> 00:18:57.386
and we did the same thing with
the ride-share driver that picked them up.

332
00:18:57.469 --> 00:18:59.721
[Hathaway] Okay. Well--

333
00:18:59.805 --> 00:19:03.475
[Hoodie Guy]
Yeah. she just got in a silver Sedan.

334
00:19:04.268 --> 00:19:06.770
[Hathaway] But you don't know
who it was or anything?

335
00:19:06.854 --> 00:19:08.856
[Hoodie Guy]
I didn't see who the driver was.

336
00:19:08.939 --> 00:19:11.900
[Anthony] The driver
that we identified later in an interview

337
00:19:11.984 --> 00:19:14.695
said when Kaylee and Maddie
got in the car. they were happy.

338
00:19:14.778 --> 00:19:16.780
They didn't seem to be upset

339
00:19:16.864 --> 00:19:20.450
or suspicious
of the individual or anything else.

340
00:19:20.534 --> 00:19:22.202
They were just having a good time.

341
00:19:22.286 --> 00:19:25.205
heading home with their food
from the Grub Truck.

342
00:19:25.289 --> 00:19:28.250
as many college students do
on a Saturday night.

343
00:19:30.002 --> 00:19:32.880
Police continue to pour through evidence
and conduct interviews.

344
00:19:32.963 --> 00:19:37.843
all to try and find out how these four
University of Idaho students were killed.

345
00:19:37.926 --> 00:19:41.597
[Brian] They're working on establishing
where everybody was that night.

346
00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:44.016
They've gotten about 500 tips so far.

347
00:19:44.099 --> 00:19:48.687
They have 22 FBI investigators that
they've brought in to help with this case.

348
00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:51.857
But for this community.
this case remains in the same place.

349
00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:55.152
No murder weapon.
no suspect. and no motive.

350
00:19:56.445 --> 00:20:00.032
Early on. people were texting me
about the story

351
00:20:00.115 --> 00:20:02.951
and said. "Have you heard
about this story in Idaho?"

352
00:20:03.035 --> 00:20:05.412
"There's these four college kids
that were murdered."

353
00:20:05.495 --> 00:20:07.080
"No one knows who did it."

354
00:20:07.164 --> 00:20:10.584
"It's really. really intense.
and I think you should get out there."

355
00:20:11.627 --> 00:20:13.712
I remember looking into it and deciding.

356
00:20:13.795 --> 00:20:16.215
"I'm gonna go to Idaho and see what's up."

357
00:20:16.798 --> 00:20:20.969
Around that same time
that the national media started arriving.

358
00:20:21.053 --> 00:20:24.890
so did the online sleuths. the YouTubers.

359
00:20:24.973 --> 00:20:27.517
and that's when the rumor mill started.

360
00:20:27.601 --> 00:20:29.561
Misinformation. speculation.

361
00:20:29.645 --> 00:20:34.441
theories fueled the flame
of everyone's imagination.

362
00:20:34.524 --> 00:20:36.068
and we were inundated.

363
00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:40.155
[Brian] At the time.
the police were not talking very much.

364
00:20:40.239 --> 00:20:42.699
and so internet sleuths. people at home.

365
00:20:42.783 --> 00:20:45.577
started trying to investigate
on their own.

366
00:20:45.661 --> 00:20:47.579
[intriguing music playing]

367
00:20:47.663 --> 00:20:51.291
[sleuth 1] So Dylan does have a boyfriend.
Just wanted to bring that up.

368
00:20:51.375 --> 00:20:54.253
I'm not saying he has anything
to do with it. Could he possibly?

369
00:20:54.336 --> 00:20:58.257
I have a theory about this Idaho 4 case
and I want people to listen to this.

370
00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:00.842
[Brian] There were just wild theories
at this point.

371
00:21:00.926 --> 00:21:04.638
And suddenly. you know.
every day there was a new theory

372
00:21:04.721 --> 00:21:06.139
about what might have happened.

373
00:21:06.223 --> 00:21:10.727
[sleuth 2] You know and I know
that crime was filmed.

374
00:21:10.811 --> 00:21:12.938
It is on the dark web.

375
00:21:13.021 --> 00:21:16.775
The physical description
of the Moscow killer was revealed to me

376
00:21:16.858 --> 00:21:20.487
in downloaded information
from the universal consciousness.

377
00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:24.324
They started trying to investigate
people from the fraternity.

378
00:21:24.408 --> 00:21:26.535
which is right across the street
from the house.

379
00:21:26.618 --> 00:21:28.829
[sleuth 3]
This is the Sigma Chi fraternity.

380
00:21:29.413 --> 00:21:33.834
This is where one of the victims.
Ethan Chapin. went to.

381
00:21:33.917 --> 00:21:35.294
Door is open.

382
00:21:35.961 --> 00:21:38.630
[Cooper] There were accusations
flying left and right.

383
00:21:39.172 --> 00:21:41.466
There were just no answers.
and so people were…

384
00:21:42.134 --> 00:21:43.552
finding answers themselves.

385
00:21:43.635 --> 00:21:47.931
[sleuth 3] If somebody from one of these
university fraternities are involved.

386
00:21:48.015 --> 00:21:50.559
university students.
and other students know.

387
00:21:50.642 --> 00:21:52.853
and they're just. they're scared.

388
00:21:52.936 --> 00:21:57.733
[Cooper] I got Facebook messages.
Twitter messages. Instagram DMs.

389
00:21:57.816 --> 00:22:01.194
all asking. what do I know?
Why aren't I saying anything?

390
00:22:01.278 --> 00:22:03.155
I got a few of those messages.

391
00:22:03.238 --> 00:22:05.157
People saying that I'm the killer.

392
00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:07.743
saying that I'm gonna get arrested.

393
00:22:07.826 --> 00:22:11.705
I'm gonna get caught. I can't
keep running. Like. what are you saying?

394
00:22:12.539 --> 00:22:15.208
[Cooper] It's hard
because all of us were processing it.

395
00:22:15.876 --> 00:22:19.379
trying to deal with our friends
that just got killed.

396
00:22:19.463 --> 00:22:21.631
and also protect ourselves
from the internet.

397
00:22:22.632 --> 00:22:25.177
[Peter] I don't understand how people
get pleasure saying that.

398
00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:28.805
I feel horrible. I can't imagine
what Dylan and Bethany get.

399
00:22:29.639 --> 00:22:30.807
It's horrible.

400
00:22:31.433 --> 00:22:33.518
[sleuth 4] Dylan Mortensen
is guilty. you guys.

401
00:22:34.394 --> 00:22:36.480
You know what she is guilty of?

402
00:22:36.563 --> 00:22:41.902
Not calling 911 for her friends.

403
00:22:42.444 --> 00:22:46.698
"How is it possible
that they wouldn't call 911 sooner?"

404
00:22:46.782 --> 00:22:48.533
"They must know something."

405
00:22:48.617 --> 00:22:53.205
There was other people in the house
when these four people are murdered.

406
00:22:53.288 --> 00:22:56.708
I 100% believe that this girl

407
00:22:56.792 --> 00:23:00.629
heard and saw so much more
than we are getting right now.

408
00:23:00.712 --> 00:23:02.339
[contemplative music playing]

409
00:23:02.422 --> 00:23:06.927
Shock and trauma
do a lot of damage to people.

410
00:23:07.010 --> 00:23:11.056
It can impair judgment.
It can impair thought processes.

411
00:23:12.099 --> 00:23:16.228
I don't blame them
for making the call a little late.

412
00:23:16.311 --> 00:23:19.856
I can only imagine
what was going through their minds.

413
00:23:19.940 --> 00:23:22.109
If it were me
in either one of their shoes.

414
00:23:22.192 --> 00:23:26.571
I would have never believed
what occurred in that house that night.

415
00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:33.245
On the phone with the coroner. we asked
if somebody would've called 911.

416
00:23:33.328 --> 00:23:35.288
-At a particular moment that night…
-Yes.

417
00:23:35.372 --> 00:23:37.499
…could Ethan have lived?
Could Xana have lived?

418
00:23:37.582 --> 00:23:39.459
Could somebody have been saved?

419
00:23:40.252 --> 00:23:42.462
And the answer was no.

420
00:23:44.005 --> 00:23:47.592
[Steve] It's hard for us. because you go
back and look at all these moments

421
00:23:47.676 --> 00:23:49.970
and you wish
you could do things different.

422
00:23:50.595 --> 00:23:52.472
And Jack felt the same way.

423
00:23:54.057 --> 00:23:56.768
[Cheryl] Jack was just lost.
you know what I mean?

424
00:23:57.352 --> 00:24:00.564
It was so hard. it was so hard on Jack
because of all the rumors.

425
00:24:01.356 --> 00:24:03.859
[Baylie] The rumors
that went around and around

426
00:24:03.942 --> 00:24:08.071
were that Jack. my cousin. had done this.

427
00:24:09.239 --> 00:24:14.286
And seeing him in this dark place
was really hard and sad.

428
00:24:14.369 --> 00:24:17.205
And then to see people online
tear him apart

429
00:24:17.289 --> 00:24:20.709
after. you know. he's already
going through what he's going through…

430
00:24:21.293 --> 00:24:22.377
Um…

431
00:24:23.170 --> 00:24:25.797
It was. it was really heartbreaking.

432
00:24:26.923 --> 00:24:28.341
[Kaylee] Jack. say hi!

433
00:24:29.009 --> 00:24:29.926
Sup?

434
00:24:31.011 --> 00:24:33.763
[Baylie] Social media got to be
kind of a more scary place

435
00:24:33.847 --> 00:24:37.225
than like… than a place
to really look for any answers.

436
00:24:37.309 --> 00:24:39.811
[melancholic music playing]

437
00:24:41.396 --> 00:24:42.856
[James] Good afternoon.

438
00:24:42.939 --> 00:24:46.193
We are thankful for all the tips
and leads the public has provided

439
00:24:46.276 --> 00:24:51.448
in Ethan. Xana. Kaylee.
and Madison's murder investigation.

440
00:24:51.990 --> 00:24:54.743
No bit of information is too small.

441
00:24:54.826 --> 00:24:56.870
and every tip will be pursued.

442
00:24:56.953 --> 00:25:00.373
We do not believe
the following individuals were involved.

443
00:25:00.874 --> 00:25:02.918
The two surviving roommates.

444
00:25:03.418 --> 00:25:08.131
the male seen in a Grub Truck video
circulating on the internet.

445
00:25:08.632 --> 00:25:11.968
a private party
who drove Kaylee and Madison home.

446
00:25:12.511 --> 00:25:16.932
any of the individuals who spoke
to the dispatcher on the 911 call.

447
00:25:17.015 --> 00:25:22.479
We're also aware of a male whom
Madison and Kaylee had called

448
00:25:22.562 --> 00:25:25.106
several times
the morning of November 13th.

449
00:25:25.190 --> 00:25:27.692
and we do not suspect that individual.

450
00:25:27.776 --> 00:25:31.446
We will continue to work hard
and continue to do everything we can.

451
00:25:31.530 --> 00:25:35.450
We want people to be vigilant. want people
to report anything suspicious to us

452
00:25:35.534 --> 00:25:36.868
and let us handle it.

453
00:25:36.952 --> 00:25:41.164
I wanna thank you today for coming.
and I appreciate your questions.

454
00:25:41.248 --> 00:25:43.500
[intriguing music playing]

455
00:25:43.583 --> 00:25:47.587
[Alivea] We were sitting
waiting for an arrest.

456
00:25:47.671 --> 00:25:50.840
Waiting for a suspect. an assailant.

457
00:25:50.924 --> 00:25:55.178
Uh. there was no information.
We had a thousand questions.

458
00:25:55.262 --> 00:25:59.558
We have no real indication of what way
this is going. Is this going cold?

459
00:25:59.641 --> 00:26:02.686
From the beginning. Steve took
the reins and said. "We're fighting."

460
00:26:02.769 --> 00:26:04.145
"We are not letting this die down."

461
00:26:04.229 --> 00:26:06.606
"We're going to make sure
there is attention on this case."

462
00:26:06.690 --> 00:26:10.235
"We are going to make sure
that we scream to the rooftop."

463
00:26:10.318 --> 00:26:14.239
I don't know how you catch a criminal
if you don't know what you're looking for.

464
00:26:14.322 --> 00:26:17.659
[news anchor] Steven Goncalves
sharing his fear and frustration.

465
00:26:18.243 --> 00:26:21.288
not only facing the heartbreaking loss
of his daughter Kaylee

466
00:26:21.371 --> 00:26:22.747
and her three friends.

467
00:26:22.831 --> 00:26:25.709
but the fact that their killer
is still at large.

468
00:26:25.792 --> 00:26:30.380
It's gonna be a cold case if we don't
do something within the next week or two.

469
00:26:30.880 --> 00:26:35.719
The amount of damage something like this
does to a family is inexcusable.

470
00:26:35.802 --> 00:26:39.889
As a dad. you wanna come that much harder
on the person who's responsible.

471
00:26:39.973 --> 00:26:42.142
You didn't do it once.
you didn't do it twice.

472
00:26:42.225 --> 00:26:44.227
you didn't do it three.
you did four times.

473
00:26:44.311 --> 00:26:47.772
And if you play God.
then we're gonna hold you accountable.

474
00:26:47.856 --> 00:26:50.859
[dramatic music playing]

475
00:26:55.739 --> 00:26:57.866
[news anchor 1]
For two weeks and two days.

476
00:26:57.949 --> 00:27:01.494
the brutal slaying
of Ethan Chapin. Madison Mogen.

477
00:27:01.578 --> 00:27:05.957
Xana Kernodle. and Kaylee Goncalves
has gone unsolved.

478
00:27:06.041 --> 00:27:10.712
[news anchor 2] Police in Moscow assure
everyone progress is being made.

479
00:27:10.795 --> 00:27:15.675
but with the killer still at large.
this fear absolutely remains.

480
00:27:17.135 --> 00:27:21.806
[Anthony] We had so much noise
coming at us from the world at large.

481
00:27:21.890 --> 00:27:23.600
Everyone's eyes are on you.

482
00:27:24.100 --> 00:27:26.770
and it can feel pretty lonely and pretty…

483
00:27:27.604 --> 00:27:31.650
When you're under that microscope.
it's tough. but we had to keep going.

484
00:27:32.984 --> 00:27:36.529
Finally. we were contacted
by the Idaho State Police lab in Meridian.

485
00:27:37.113 --> 00:27:42.118
who told us that they had found
a single-source male DNA

486
00:27:42.202 --> 00:27:43.953
from the snap on that knife sheath.

487
00:27:44.037 --> 00:27:45.538
[intriguing music playing]

488
00:27:45.622 --> 00:27:48.083
They had developed a profile
based on that.

489
00:27:48.166 --> 00:27:49.876
They put it through the CODIS system.

490
00:27:49.959 --> 00:27:52.921
which is our national DNA database.
but had received no hits.

491
00:27:53.004 --> 00:27:56.132
The DNA on the knife sheath did not match
any one particular person.

492
00:27:57.217 --> 00:27:59.135
So whose DNA is this?

493
00:27:59.844 --> 00:28:03.056
The next step was
to hand-deliver that profile

494
00:28:03.139 --> 00:28:07.560
to the Othram labs in Texas to begin
the investigative genetic genealogy.

495
00:28:08.895 --> 00:28:14.442
[Ed] Investigative genetic genealogy
takes the DNA sampling

496
00:28:14.526 --> 00:28:17.612
through commercially-available databases

497
00:28:17.696 --> 00:28:19.572
where people have submitted their DNA

498
00:28:19.656 --> 00:28:22.117
to find their family histories.

499
00:28:23.118 --> 00:28:29.040
From that. you find distant relatives.
and you start building family trees

500
00:28:29.124 --> 00:28:35.922
to try to come up with a group of suspects
from an unknown DNA sample.

501
00:28:36.715 --> 00:28:41.010
It was very exciting that we had
a new development in the case.

502
00:28:42.137 --> 00:28:44.222
but we couldn't hang our hat on that.

503
00:28:44.806 --> 00:28:48.101
So as soon as the lab received that item.
they went to work.

504
00:28:48.184 --> 00:28:49.769
but we kept working on our end.

505
00:28:54.065 --> 00:28:55.942
In the initial canvassing of the area

506
00:28:56.025 --> 00:28:59.946
was actually when we recognized that there
was a camera on the neighboring home.

507
00:29:00.029 --> 00:29:01.948
-[detective 1] You have a camera.
-[woman 1] Yes.

508
00:29:02.031 --> 00:29:04.534
-[detective 1] Have other cameras?
-[woman 1] Just that one.

509
00:29:04.617 --> 00:29:08.413
-[detective 1] How big? Mind if I see?
-[woman 1] The road. it cuts out…

510
00:29:08.496 --> 00:29:09.914
[woman 2] Just the driveway.

511
00:29:09.998 --> 00:29:12.125
Our detectives recognized that immediately

512
00:29:12.208 --> 00:29:15.211
and seized that camera
and all of its components.

513
00:29:15.295 --> 00:29:17.630
brought that back to the department
and started working.

514
00:29:17.714 --> 00:29:20.300
-[woman 1] Here's the SD card.
-[detective 2] I appreciate that.

515
00:29:20.383 --> 00:29:22.177
-[woman 1] Of course.
-[detective 3] Thank you.

516
00:29:22.260 --> 00:29:24.471
Video is considered vanishing evidence.

517
00:29:24.554 --> 00:29:27.974
Different cameras have different
write-over times.

518
00:29:28.057 --> 00:29:30.477
different save times.
and you don't know what that is.

519
00:29:30.560 --> 00:29:34.981
So. it's very critical you get all video
footage you can

520
00:29:35.064 --> 00:29:36.441
as fast as possible.

521
00:29:37.275 --> 00:29:40.945
[Anthony] Our detectives
who had seized the neighbor's camera

522
00:29:41.696 --> 00:29:44.282
had been able
to more or less get into the system.

523
00:29:44.365 --> 00:29:48.828
And initially. they were only able
to retrieve video. there was no audio.

524
00:29:48.912 --> 00:29:52.749
But they were eventually able to combine
the two and get the video and audio.

525
00:29:55.543 --> 00:29:58.171
It was very clear
that we had something here.

526
00:29:58.254 --> 00:30:00.799
[dramatic music playing]

527
00:30:03.301 --> 00:30:06.137
Starting in the early hours of the 13th.

528
00:30:06.221 --> 00:30:11.100
this white car is seen
in the area of 1122 King Road.

529
00:30:13.186 --> 00:30:15.396
We see it come and go from the area.

530
00:30:15.480 --> 00:30:18.107
sometimes a little bit slowly.
several times.

531
00:30:19.234 --> 00:30:23.363
[Ed] Between approximately 3:30 a.m.
and 4:06 a.m..

532
00:30:23.446 --> 00:30:28.660
the vehicle is seen entering
and leaving the area four times.

533
00:30:28.743 --> 00:30:32.121
[Anthony] And then
the final time. at 4:20 a.m.

534
00:30:32.205 --> 00:30:34.207
[dog barking]

535
00:30:40.255 --> 00:30:42.090
[tires screech]

536
00:30:43.258 --> 00:30:47.470
This white car is seen again on the camera
leaving at a high rate of speed.

537
00:30:47.554 --> 00:30:51.891
almost seemingly crashing
on the way out of the neighborhood.

538
00:30:52.725 --> 00:30:55.228
Prior to the car leaving the area.

539
00:30:55.311 --> 00:30:59.023
Xana's phone records show
that she had ordered a DoorDash.

540
00:30:59.107 --> 00:31:01.860
and that DoorDash was delivered
at approximately 4:00 a.m.

541
00:31:04.279 --> 00:31:09.409
She was awake. scrolling on social media.
up until about 4:12 in the morning.

542
00:31:10.034 --> 00:31:15.498
So we know that between 4:12.
when Xana is awake and active.

543
00:31:15.582 --> 00:31:20.420
and 4:20. when that vehicle is speeding
out of the area for the last time.

544
00:31:21.421 --> 00:31:24.132
during that time frame.
these murders occurred.

545
00:31:26.634 --> 00:31:29.053
This is our person. This is our suspect.

546
00:31:31.890 --> 00:31:35.810
You can't see much detail
in a car on a camera at night

547
00:31:35.894 --> 00:31:41.524
because headlights. taillights wash out
most of the detail of the car.

548
00:31:42.025 --> 00:31:45.111
[Anthony] Our investigators sent out
that video to the FBI.

549
00:31:45.194 --> 00:31:47.155
where they have vehicle experts.

550
00:31:47.238 --> 00:31:51.326
We also found surveillance footage
from other areas around Moscow.

551
00:31:51.409 --> 00:31:56.456
[Ed] They look at details of it.
window shape. size. comparisons.

552
00:31:56.539 --> 00:31:59.417
And they could only narrow it down

553
00:31:59.500 --> 00:32:04.339
to three or four different makes
and models that it could have been.

554
00:32:05.465 --> 00:32:10.470
As we were getting more vehicle feed.
we would send clips to them

555
00:32:10.553 --> 00:32:14.557
to determine if we could develop
a make. model. and year.

556
00:32:15.099 --> 00:32:19.354
We got some distance video
from an apartment complex.

557
00:32:19.437 --> 00:32:23.232
Another residential camera
a couple miles away.

558
00:32:23.316 --> 00:32:24.817
We got taillights.

559
00:32:25.401 --> 00:32:28.071
So. they started adding that
to the collection

560
00:32:28.154 --> 00:32:30.281
to try to narrow down the vehicle.

561
00:32:30.365 --> 00:32:34.494
And we finally got a clear shot

562
00:32:34.577 --> 00:32:40.166
of a side profile of the vehicle
under a streetlight.

563
00:32:40.249 --> 00:32:42.877
It wasn't washed out by its own lights.

564
00:32:45.088 --> 00:32:48.800
The vehicle identification analyst

565
00:32:48.883 --> 00:32:52.345
was able at that point to say.

566
00:32:52.428 --> 00:32:57.767
this is a Hyundai Elantra
between the years of 2011 to 2016.

567
00:32:59.102 --> 00:33:01.354
And then on December 19th.

568
00:33:01.437 --> 00:33:07.360
we received a call from the FBI's
investigative genealogical team.

569
00:33:07.443 --> 00:33:09.529
and the team leader said.

570
00:33:10.613 --> 00:33:11.739
"We have a name."

571
00:33:12.907 --> 00:33:14.158
"Bryan Kohberger."

572
00:33:14.283 --> 00:33:15.868
[intriguing music playing]

573
00:33:15.952 --> 00:33:20.373
He attends Washington State University
and he drives a white Hyundai Elantra.

574
00:33:20.456 --> 00:33:23.626
[man] Lincoln. Frank. Zebra. 8-6-4-9.

575
00:33:24.252 --> 00:33:27.505
[Ed] We opened up the investigation
into Bryan Kohberger.

576
00:33:28.089 --> 00:33:30.925
[Anthony] And we started getting
information immediately.

577
00:33:31.884 --> 00:33:33.261
-[deputy] Hey there.
-Hi.

578
00:33:33.344 --> 00:33:36.681
I stopped you going a little fast.
Do you realize this is. uh. 35?

579
00:33:36.764 --> 00:33:39.058
-Oh. it's 35?
-It is. yeah. So you were going--

580
00:33:39.142 --> 00:33:41.853
-About 41?
-Yeah. 43 was what the radar said.

581
00:33:41.936 --> 00:33:46.149
Immediately. we found a deputy
had pulled Kohberger over one evening

582
00:33:46.232 --> 00:33:50.361
in a white Hyundai Elantra for.
I believe. a speeding violation.

583
00:33:50.445 --> 00:33:53.489
and ended up issuing him a citation
for not wearing a seat belt.

584
00:33:53.573 --> 00:33:58.745
Because of that citation. we had the cell
phone number belonging to Kohberger.

585
00:33:58.828 --> 00:34:01.622
which was utilized
in obtaining search warrants

586
00:34:01.706 --> 00:34:03.624
and getting cell phone data.

587
00:34:04.125 --> 00:34:06.878
-[deputy] Can I get a phone number?
-Yeah. why?

588
00:34:06.961 --> 00:34:10.757
Uh. we need to put it on the citation
as it goes to the court.

589
00:34:12.425 --> 00:34:16.304
[Anthony] One of the first things we saw
was his phone had pinged off of towers

590
00:34:16.387 --> 00:34:18.347
that service the area of Moscow

591
00:34:18.431 --> 00:34:22.185
many times over the course
of several months

592
00:34:22.268 --> 00:34:24.687
prior to the November 13th incident.

593
00:34:25.813 --> 00:34:29.609
His typical pathway
from his residence in Pullman was.

594
00:34:29.692 --> 00:34:33.196
as most people here would use.
is the Moscow-Pullman highway.

595
00:34:36.032 --> 00:34:38.826
It's the direct link
between Pullman and Moscow.

596
00:34:41.204 --> 00:34:44.749
And we could see that he'd made
several trips into Moscow to shop.

597
00:34:44.832 --> 00:34:47.710
We had cell phone data
of him in local stores.

598
00:34:48.503 --> 00:34:51.547
It's not out of the ordinary
for college students to do that.

599
00:34:51.631 --> 00:34:55.218
especially with WSU and University
of Idaho being so close together.

600
00:34:55.301 --> 00:34:57.970
[ominous music playing]

601
00:34:58.054 --> 00:35:00.848
But when we started narrowing in
on King Road.

602
00:35:02.517 --> 00:35:05.937
we saw his phone
in that area multiple times.

603
00:35:07.355 --> 00:35:10.191
Very odd hours. late at night.

604
00:35:10.274 --> 00:35:12.985
That really started
linking things together.

605
00:35:16.989 --> 00:35:18.825
On the night of the murders.

606
00:35:20.618 --> 00:35:23.037
November 12th into the 13th.

607
00:35:24.455 --> 00:35:27.083
at approximately 2:42 a.m..

608
00:35:28.918 --> 00:35:31.295
Kohberger's phone was connecting
to cell phone towers

609
00:35:31.379 --> 00:35:34.173
that serviced his residence in Pullman.

610
00:35:35.299 --> 00:35:36.843
[car engine starts]

611
00:35:36.926 --> 00:35:38.594
At approximately 2:47.

612
00:35:40.304 --> 00:35:43.850
he left his residence.
began moving south through Pullman.

613
00:35:46.310 --> 00:35:48.563
Kohberger's phone then went dark.

614
00:35:49.438 --> 00:35:50.731
It was shortly after that

615
00:35:50.815 --> 00:35:54.235
the white Elantra enters
the area of the crime scene.

616
00:35:54.735 --> 00:35:58.656
During that time frame is when we know
that these murders occurred.

617
00:36:02.994 --> 00:36:04.620
At approximately 4:48.

618
00:36:04.704 --> 00:36:08.166
Kohberger's phone reactivates
onto cellular data.

619
00:36:08.249 --> 00:36:12.086
and it is seen being south of Moscow
on Highway 95.

620
00:36:12.170 --> 00:36:14.005
[contemplative music playing]

621
00:36:14.797 --> 00:36:17.133
And then at approximately 5:30 a.m..

622
00:36:17.216 --> 00:36:19.760
Kohberger's phone is seen connecting

623
00:36:19.844 --> 00:36:22.638
to a cell phone tower again
near his residence.

624
00:36:24.849 --> 00:36:29.478
[Ed] The loop where he's left the house
from that area and going into farmland

625
00:36:29.562 --> 00:36:31.856
and coming up on the south side of Pullman

626
00:36:31.939 --> 00:36:35.735
took about an hour and ten minutes
for him to get back.

627
00:36:36.319 --> 00:36:40.448
It was a bit odd.
but when you think about it.

628
00:36:40.531 --> 00:36:45.036
a KA-BAR knife. even though
it's a rather large knife or as knives go.

629
00:36:45.119 --> 00:36:46.579
it's a small object.

630
00:36:46.662 --> 00:36:49.707
And there's an insurmountable
amount of places

631
00:36:49.790 --> 00:36:52.335
where something like that could end up.

632
00:36:57.089 --> 00:36:58.925
What we really found interesting was

633
00:36:59.008 --> 00:37:01.302
immediately after November 13th.

634
00:37:02.094 --> 00:37:05.848
Bryan Kohberger never came back
to Moscow as he did prior.

635
00:37:07.725 --> 00:37:12.730
We also found through search warrants
for his credit cards and his financials

636
00:37:12.813 --> 00:37:16.734
that he had stopped coming to Moscow
buying anything. period.

637
00:37:16.817 --> 00:37:23.699
So this very starkly different behavior
after November 13th started to develop.

638
00:37:23.783 --> 00:37:25.785
[contemplative music continues]

639
00:37:28.704 --> 00:37:33.793
[Ed] At this point. Bryan Kohberger
becomes our suspect in the case.

640
00:37:33.876 --> 00:37:39.757
but investigative genealogy
is not court-admissible evidence.

641
00:37:39.840 --> 00:37:46.138
We knew that we needed to be able to link
the DNA on that knife sheath to Kohberger.

642
00:37:46.222 --> 00:37:48.224
[police siren blares]

643
00:37:48.307 --> 00:37:51.018
[Ed] Once we started running checks.

644
00:37:51.560 --> 00:37:54.605
we learned that on December 15th.

645
00:37:54.689 --> 00:37:59.235
Bryan had been pulled over
in the Elantra twice in Indiana

646
00:37:59.318 --> 00:38:02.280
for following vehicles too close.

647
00:38:02.363 --> 00:38:05.533
-[officer 1] Hello. How y'all doing today?
-How you doing?

648
00:38:06.075 --> 00:38:09.870
[officer 1] Good. good.
So you was right up on that van. man.

649
00:38:09.954 --> 00:38:12.206
[Ed] His father
was in the vehicle with him.

650
00:38:13.165 --> 00:38:15.876
[officer 1] You're coming
from Washington State University?

651
00:38:15.960 --> 00:38:18.504
-Yeah.
-[officer 1] And you're going where?

652
00:38:18.587 --> 00:38:21.299
-We're gonna be going to Pennsylvania.
-[officer 1] Okay.

653
00:38:21.382 --> 00:38:24.427
[Ed] We determined
that he was traveling back

654
00:38:24.510 --> 00:38:26.929
to his parents' house in Pennsylvania.

655
00:38:29.557 --> 00:38:32.560
[Anthony] The house was relatively normal

656
00:38:32.643 --> 00:38:34.687
on a quiet. little street.

657
00:38:34.770 --> 00:38:37.648
We worked with our FBI partners back east.

658
00:38:37.732 --> 00:38:42.862
and they immediately started surveilling
the residence and Kohberger himself.

659
00:38:42.945 --> 00:38:45.281
[suspenseful music playing]

660
00:38:45.364 --> 00:38:46.782
They did witness some.

661
00:38:46.866 --> 00:38:49.952
for lack of a better term.
strange behavior.

662
00:38:50.036 --> 00:38:51.996
He was seen both in the home

663
00:38:52.079 --> 00:38:54.790
and outside the home in public
wearing rubber gloves.

664
00:38:55.958 --> 00:38:59.337
[Ed] Any time he would leave the house.
the FBI were attempting

665
00:38:59.420 --> 00:39:01.922
to find what we call "discarded DNA."

666
00:39:02.006 --> 00:39:06.135
Something that somebody leaves behind
that would contain their DNA

667
00:39:06.218 --> 00:39:10.890
that can be collected
by the surveillance agents.

668
00:39:12.058 --> 00:39:16.187
But during the course of a week.
he only left the house three times.

669
00:39:18.564 --> 00:39:23.194
So it was decided to do what
in law enforcement we call a "trash pull."

670
00:39:23.277 --> 00:39:25.196
When trash is put out to the curb.

671
00:39:25.279 --> 00:39:27.698
it's considered abandoned at that point.

672
00:39:27.782 --> 00:39:32.119
and we can legally seize that trash

673
00:39:32.203 --> 00:39:33.662
and… and collect it.

674
00:39:38.042 --> 00:39:40.669
On Tuesday the 27th.
we knew it was trash day.

675
00:39:41.796 --> 00:39:44.173
The agent arrived at 4:00 a.m.

676
00:39:44.256 --> 00:39:47.510
to confirm the trash was there
before grabbing it.

677
00:39:47.593 --> 00:39:51.972
and Bryan was actually walking
down the street at that time.

678
00:39:52.640 --> 00:39:56.685
The agent called me up and said. "I just
saw Bryan walking down the street."

679
00:39:58.687 --> 00:40:00.189
We collected the trash.

680
00:40:01.399 --> 00:40:04.026
Any items that could have contained DNA

681
00:40:04.110 --> 00:40:05.986
were collected from that trash

682
00:40:06.070 --> 00:40:09.990
and all that evidence arrived
at the Idaho State Police lab at 1:00 a.m.

683
00:40:10.074 --> 00:40:14.286
They had all of their technicians in
and started processing that evidence.

684
00:40:15.913 --> 00:40:19.458
We found a Q-tip
within that trash that was tested.

685
00:40:19.542 --> 00:40:25.005
and it tested that the DNA on that Q-tip

686
00:40:25.089 --> 00:40:30.261
belonged to the father of the person
whose DNA was on that knife sheath.

687
00:40:31.345 --> 00:40:35.141
There was only one male son
in that family.

688
00:40:35.224 --> 00:40:36.475
It was Bryan Kohberger.

689
00:40:37.852 --> 00:40:38.853
We had him.

690
00:40:40.104 --> 00:40:44.483
[woman] I got the notification on my phone
that the Idaho perpetrator was arrested.

691
00:40:45.234 --> 00:40:48.320
I pull up a picture.
and I almost passed out.

692
00:40:48.404 --> 00:40:50.322
I felt the blood leave my face.

693
00:40:50.406 --> 00:40:52.241
I was horrified.

694
